    "['family inet [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 800', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 800'], 'root': 'router bgp 800', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco configuration command for the given Juniper BGP family configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 800\\n neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100\\n neighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The autonomous-system 800 from the Juniper config is included as it's required for the BGP context in Cisco\\n2. The neighbor remote-as command is included as it's required before setting address-family\\n3. Cisco automatically enables IPv4 unicast by default in recent IOS versions, but explicitly configuring it matches the Juniper intent\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 800'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 800'], 'root': 'router bgp 800', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco configuration command for the given Juniper BGP family configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 800\\n neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100\\n neighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The autonomous-system 800 from the Juniper config is included as it's required for the BGP context in Cisco\\n2. The neighbor remote-as command is included as it's required before setting address-family\\n3. Cisco automatically enables IPv4 unicast by default in recent IOS versions, but explicitly configuring it matches the Juniper intent\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 800'], 'root': 'router bgp 800', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco configuration command for the given Juniper BGP family configuration:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 800\\n neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100\\n neighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The autonomous-system 800 from the Juniper config is included as it's required for the BGP context in Cisco\\n2. The neighbor remote-as command is included as it's required before setting address-family\\n3. Cisco automatically enables IPv4 unicast by default in recent IOS versions, but explicitly configuring it matches the Juniper intent\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast'}]]": 1,
    "['neighbor [parameter2] family inet unicast', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast', 'parent_command': ['router bgp 800'], 'root': 'router bgp 800', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the given Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\nneighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Cisco IOS, BGP address-family configuration is typically done under the router bgp context, and the exact syntax may vary slightly depending on IOS version. The above command assumes you're already in the appropriate BGP configuration mode (router bgp 800) and neighbor configuration context.\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 address-family ipv4 unicast'}]]": 1,
