    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'router bgp 800', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'router bgp 800', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command `set protocols bgp group BGP_GROUP neighbor 10.3.1.2 peer-as 100` to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 800\\nneighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The autonomous-system 800 from Juniper becomes the `router bgp 800` context in Cisco\\n2. The neighbor peer-as configuration becomes `neighbor [ip] remote-as [asn]` in Cisco\\n3. In Cisco, BGP configuration is entered in router configuration mode, hence the two commands\", 'trans_template': 'router bgp 800'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command `set protocols bgp group BGP_GROUP neighbor 10.3.1.2 peer-as 100` to Cisco IOS:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 800\\nneighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. The autonomous-system 800 from Juniper becomes the `router bgp 800` context in Cisco\\n2. The neighbor peer-as configuration becomes `neighbor [ip] remote-as [asn]` in Cisco\\n3. In Cisco, BGP configuration is entered in router configuration mode, hence the two commands\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 10.3.1.2 remote-as 100'}]]": 1,
